      "q": "[SQL Interview Questions Advanced #3] When evaluating edge-case safety in 'SQL Interview Questions', suppose an algorithm computes the midpoint of two 32-bit signed integers `low` and `high` where `low = 1,500,000,000` and `high = 1,800,000,000`. Why does the standard expression `mid = (low + high) / 2` fail, and what is the standard fix?",
