      "h": "Count unique pairs of (i, j) within grid dimensions.",
      "e": "With memoization, each state defined by (i, j) where 0 <= i < N and 0 <= j < M is computed exactly once. There are N * M unique states, and each state performs O(1) work (two recursive lookups and an addition). Hence, total subproblems is O(N * M) and overall time complexity is O(N * M).",
      "step": "Step 1: State space = { (i, j) | 0 <= i < N, 0 <= j < M }.\nStep 2: Size of state space = |S| = N * M.\nStep 3: Transition cost per state = O(1) arithmetic operations.\nStep 4: Total complexity = |S| * O(1) = O(N * M).",
      "tech": "Dynamic programming state-space complexity formulation.",
      "formula": "\\text{Time} = |\\text{States}| \\times \\text{Cost per state} = O(N \\times M) \\times O(1) = O(N M)",
