      "difficulty": "Hard",
      "q": "[Python Statistical and Mathematical Operations Advanced #1] In 'Python Statistical and Mathematical Operations', you are tasked with optimizing memory cache performance for an array matrix of size 14 x 14. When traversing the matrix in C/C++, why does row-major order (`arr[i][j]`) demonstrate significantly higher throughput than column-major order (`arr[j][i]`)?",
